 "final_summary": "The bug was caused by using floor division (//) instead of regular division (/) in the average_priority calculation, which truncated decimal values. The fix replaced // with / in tracker/services.py, ensuring fractional values like 8/3=2.67 are correctly computed and preserved. Both the reproduction test and the full test suite now pass.",
